      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "The effects of serum bilirubin on blood lipids and lipoproteins in 237 subjects were investigated. The findings were that total cholesterol (TC) and low density lipoprotein-cholesterol (LDL-C) were negatively correlated with total bilirubin and direct bilirubin. The results indicate that bilirubin affects metabolism of lipoproteins and the low level of serum bilirubin is a new risk factor for coronary heart disease."},
